# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/

# Docker override. Local by design: compose auto-loads it, so a committed one
# would silently switch every user off the published image and onto a
# build-from-source dev stack. Copy compose.override.yaml.dist to create it.
compose.override.yaml
docker-compose.override.yml

# Mutex directory for the one-time `composer install` in the dev entrypoint.
/.composer-install.lock/

# Symfony CLI reads a php.ini here and passes it to the PHP-FPM behind
# `symfony serve`. CI writes one (a copy of frankenphp/conf.d/10-app.ini) so the
# local server gets the same upload limits as the Docker image. Committing one
# would override those limits for everyone, from a file nothing points at.
/php.ini

truenas.compose.yaml.local

